title: "June Poem - June Amongst the Roses"
poemTitle: "June Poem - June Amongst the Roses"
author: "Eila Webster"
bgTheme: "antiquewhite"
endOfYear: false
---
<div class="full-width">
<poem-grid :title="poemTitle" :author="author" :theme="bgTheme">

  <!-- Header Section -->
  <img src="/poems/june-poem-june-amongst-the-roses/image-0.png" alt="" slot="header-tl" />
  <img src="/poems/june-poem-june-amongst-the-roses/image-1.png" alt="" slot="header-tr" />

  <!-- Column 1 Images (15%) -->
  <div slot="col-1-images">
    <img src="/poems/june-poem-june-amongst-the-roses/image-6.png" alt="" />
    <img src="/poems/june-poem-june-amongst-the-roses/image-8.png" alt="" />
  </div>

  <!-- Column 2 Text -->
  <div slot="col-2-text">
    <p>
      June is a romantic month
      Filled with the sight and scent of roses,
      When males splash out on a bunch
      then on bended knee proposes.
    </p>

    <p>
      Weddings too take centre stage
      As the sun shines on bride and groom;
      A perfect time for holidays
      Or to have a honeymoon.
    </p>

    <p>
      Yet we should not forget the rain
      that sneaks in to wreck what is planned;
      But without its presence in our lives
      We wouldn’t have a lush green fertile land.
    </p>

    <p>
      The envy of all our neighbours
      In their dry baked summers o’er the sea;
      As we sit outside in a dappled shade
      of some large bushes or a tree.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Column 3 Middle Images -->
  <div slot="col-3-images">
    <img src="/poems/june-poem-june-amongst-the-roses/image-2.png" alt="" />
    <img src="/poems/june-poem-june-amongst-the-roses/image-3.png" alt="" />
    <img src="/poems/june-poem-june-amongst-the-roses/image-4.png" alt="" />
  </div>

  <!-- Column 4 Text -->
  <div slot="col-4-text">
    <p>
      ***
      If you choose to go and chase the sun
      And leave all this beauty behind;
      Things may not live up to expectations
    </p>

    <p>
      There could be many snags to find.
      You’ll soon tire of all this constant heat
      Dry colourless deserts and burning sand;
      You’ll be glad to be back amongst the roses
    </p>

    <p>
      In June’s fragrant dew spangled land.
      Coming in the middle of the year
      June really does hold the key;
      When you are looking for perfection
    </p>
  </div>

